''[[Catfish: The TV Show]]'' is an American television series that began airing on [[MTV]] on November 12, 2012.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://zap2it.com/2012/08/catfish-the-tv-show-mtv-delves-into-online-relationships/|title='Catfish: The TV Show': MTV delves into online relationships|first=Rick|last=Porter|work=Zap2it|date=August 3, 2012|access-date=February 28, 2016|archive-date=February 21, 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160221215543/http://zap2it.com/2012/08/catfish-the-tv-show-mtv-delves-into-online-relationships/|url-status=dead}}</ref> The second season began airing on June 25, 2013.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2013/06/26/tuesday-cable-ratings-catfish-rizzoli-isles-win-night-pretty-little-liars-deadliest-catch-perception-more/189108/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130629160817/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2013/06/26/tuesday-cable-ratings-catfish-rizzoli-isles-win-night-pretty-little-liars-deadliest-catch-perception-more/189108/|url-status=dead|archive-date=June 29, 2013|title=Tuesday Cable Ratings: 'Catfish' & 'Rizzoli & Isles' Win Night, 'Pretty Little Liars', 'Deadliest Catch', 'Perception' & More|first=Sara|last=Bibel|work=Zap2it|date=June 26, 2013|access-date=February 28, 2016}}</ref> Season 3 and Season 4 premiered respectively on May 7, 2014, and February 25, 2015.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.people.com/article/catfish-season-three-premiere-recap-craig-zoe-nev-schulman|title=Catfish Season Premiere Recap: Meet the First 'Catfish Terrorist'|first=Kelli|last=Bender|work=people.com|date=May 8, 2014|access-date=February 28, 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/02/26/wednesday-cable-ratings-catfish-tops-night-mob-wives-the-game-house-hunters-more/367779/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150227004030/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/02/26/wednesday-cable-ratings-catfish-tops-night-mob-wives-the-game-house-hunters-more/367779/|url-status=dead|archive-date=February 27, 2015|title=Wednesday Cable Ratings: 'Catfish' Tops Night + 'Mob Wives', 'The Game', 'House Hunters' & More|first=Seve|last=Baron|work=Zap2it|date=February 26, 2015|access-date=February 28, 2016}}</ref> Season 5 began airing on February 24, 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2016/02/25/wednesday-cable-ratings-feb-24-2016/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160226101534/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2016/02/25/wednesday-cable-ratings-feb-24-2016/|url-status=dead|archive-date=February 26, 2016|title=Wednesday cable ratings: 'Broad City' falls, 'Mob Wives' stays steady|last=Kondolojy|first=Amanda|work=TV by the Numbers|date=February 25, 2016|access-date=February 28, 2016}}</ref> Season 8 premiered on January 8, 2020.<ref>{{Cite web|title='Who's Ready to go Fishing?': Catfish Returns with new Twists -- and new Lies|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/3148658/catfish-first-look-lies-twists/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191213053812/http://www.mtv.com/news/3148658/catfish-first-look-lies-twists/|url-status=dead|archive-date=December 13, 2019|work=[[MTV News]]|access-date=2019-12-14|language=en}}</ref> The second part of the eighth season premiered on August 5, 2020, and featured the first episodes of the series where the hosts only interacted online instead of in person because of the [[COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref>{{cite web|title=MTV's "Catfish: The TV Show" Makes Epic Return with Its First-Ever Virtual Season Premiering Wednesday, August 5th at 8PM ET/PT|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2020/07/08/mtvs-catfish-the-tv-show-makes-epic-return-with-its-first-ever-virtual-season-premiering-wednesday-august-5th-at-8pm-et-pt-524314/20200708mtv01/|work=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=July 8, 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=CATFISH: THE TV SHOW TO RETURN -- AND IT'S 'GOING GLOBAL'|url=https://www.mtv.com/news/3183065/catfish-return-global/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211215194116/http://www.mtv.com/news/3183065/catfish-return-global/|url-status=dead|archive-date=December 15, 2021|work=MTV News|date=December 15, 2021}}</ref>

